F1: Game class holds state; mulberry32(seed) used for terrain/colonists/events/storms/trade; endTurn() fixed order. Score 2.

F2: 8x8 map loop; generateTerrain(rng,x,y); canBuild checks building.terrain.includes(tile.terrain); adjacency loop multiplies `produce` in produceResources(). Score 2.

F3: FORGE ore→metal, GREENHOUSE ash→soil→food conversions; storage_capacity overflow trimmed in produceResources(). Score 2.

F4: skills read via `skill_bonus = c.skills[building.skill]` in produceResources, but `fatigue` only incremented/decremented, never read to affect output. Score 1.

F5: consumption loop drops food/water; shortage sets morale -=5; but produceResources() formula never reads `morale`, so morale never changes output. Score 1.

F6: RESEARCH_TREE has 8 nodes; canResearch enforces prereqs/cost; doResearch only applies effects for 4/8 ids (ore_refining, irrigation, power_grid, shelter_tech) — advanced_forge/soil_science/preservation/advanced_lab have no effect code. Score 1.

F7: 10 EVENTS; fireEvent() does weighted pick + cooldown via fired_events; but outcome is chosen by `rng()`, not a player choice — "choices" are never presented to the user. Score 1.

F8: updateTradeState() drifts trade_supply and reads resources for pricing; buyResource/sellResource work; no caravan inventory cap exists anywhere. Score 1.

F9: triggerAshstorm() reduces tile.building_health, health_factor multiplies output in produceResources(); shelter_tech raises storm_damage_reduction; but no repair function exists anywhere — building_health never recovers. Score 1.

F10: serialize()/deserialize() round-trip most state (event_log omitted); loadGame() try/catch shows alert on bad input. Score 2.

F11: win check (turn>=60 && pop>=12 && resources) and lose check (colonists.length===0) both in endTurn(); calculateScore() combines pop/research/scrip/turn; renderGameOverModal() shown. Score 2.

F12: switchTab() wired to tab buttons; log() stores turn, shown in renderEventsTab; title attributes on tiles/buildings; keydown listener for Space/1-6; @media(max-width:600px) CSS. Score 2.

F13: runTests() has 15 substantive invariant checks (morale bounds, save/load roundtrip, prereqs); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless endTurn() calls and prints state_hash. Score 2.

G1: doResearch() for ore_refining/irrigation/power_grid gives one-time resource bump only; produceResources() never reads research_done to modify per-turn yield formula. Score 0.

G2: shortage writes colonist.morale -=5, but produceResources() formula ignores morale; only effect is colonist removal at morale<=0 (special-case labor loss). Score 2.

G3: triggerAshstorm() damages tile.building_health; health_factor reduces produceResources() output; but no repair function exists anywhere, so damage is permanent and recovery/repair-cost link is entirely missing. Score 1.

G4: updateTradeState() drifts trade_supply(rng) and applies `resources[res]>200` stockpile discount into trade_prices, read by buy/sellResource; runs only every caravan cycle. Score 3.

G5: settler_arrival ("Welcome": +colonist,-food vs "Turn away": nothing) and equipment_malfunction ("Repair":-parts vs "Postpone":-power) durably diverge state, not just log. Score 4.

